.TH SAPHIRA-AGENTS 8 "October 2026" "Saphira Linux" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
saphira-agents \- install coding agents and provider SDKs from npm
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B saphira-agents
.RI [ --setup " | " --list " | " --installed " | " --update " | " --help ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B saphira-agents
installs terminal coding agents and model provider SDKs: npm
packages, vendor standalone release artefacts (hash-verified), and
PyPI packages where a backend exists. Only agents proven to install
and execute on Saphira appear; anything else is omitted rather than
offered. It is the operator-driven,
interactive front to the fast-moving npm agent ecosystem; the stable
Saphira foundation underneath it is the
.BR saphira-agents (7)
meta-package.
.PP
Every run starts by choosing a scope. Per-user scope (the default)
installs under
.IR $HOME/.local .
Global scope installs machine-wide into
.I /usr
and requires root; its binaries are shared by all users while each
user's authentication, configuration and sessions stay per-user.
Some packages restrict which scopes are offered: Claude Code, for
example, is per-user-only because Anthropic warns against installing
it with sudo npm.
.PP
Install policy is per package, not uniform. Packages whose postinstall
step was inspected and proven necessary carry a narrow
.I --allow-scripts=<package>
approval; packages with no lifecycle scripts install plainly. There
is no blanket script approval. The same policy drives initial
installs and
.B --update
runs alike.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR --setup
Run the interactive installer (per-user scope by default; global
scope under root where package policy permits it).
.TP
.BR --list
Show installable selections with their npm package names, permitted
scopes, and script-approval notes.
.TP
.BR --installed
Show packages recorded by saphira-agents, per scope, cross-checked
against what is actually present (a manually removed package reads
"(missing)").
.TP
.BR --update
Reinstall every recorded package of the current context (global when
run as root, per-user otherwise) at its current upstream release,
using the same per-package policy as installation.
.TP
.BR --help ", " -h
Show usage and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/saphira-agents/state
Global install records: timestamp, scope, selection, npm package,
installed version.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/saphira-agents/state
Per-user install records, same format.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success (including "nothing selected" and "nothing recorded").
.TP
.B 1
Usage error, validation failure, refused scope, or at least one
package operation failed.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Install interactively (per-user default):
.B saphira-agents --setup
.TP
Install machine-wide (as root):
.B sudo saphira-agents --setup
.TP
Audit and refresh:
.B saphira-agents --installed
.br
.B saphira-agents --update
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR npm (1)
.PP
Upstream install requirements change; the encoded per-package policy
reflects what was inspected at packaging time. Provider credentials
are never stored or configured by this tool.
